course: dictionary
lesson: 934
title: Slang and shiny words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slang is informal words people use in everyday talk, often with friends. You will not find every slang word in a school book, so context clues help a lot. «Her phone case is covered in bling.» The word bling sits next to phone case, so it must mean something shiny or sparkly.
explain: Bling can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun, it means shiny, expensive-looking jewellery, like big gold chains and sparkly rings: «He wore so much bling to the party.» As an adjective, it means flashy or covered in sparkles: «a bling dance costume».
explain: Slang can also tell you about a person. «He can't stop talking about his car, all bling and chains.» The writer is not only describing the car. The word shows he wants people to see that he has money, so he is showing off.
explain: Words change from place to place. In the UK, «quid» means pounds. In Ireland, «grand» means fine. In a friendly chat, «my guy» means mate. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: Slang is informal language used in everyday talk, not usually in formal writing.
fact: «Bling» means shiny, expensive-looking jewellery, such as big gold chains and sparkly rings.
fact: «Bling» can also mean a flashy show of wealth, or something covered in glitter or sparkles.
fact: «Bling-bling» is a phrase used to describe something very sparkly or flashy.
fact: Some slang comes from particular places: «quid» (UK) means pounds, and «grand» (Ireland) means fine.
exercise: «Her new trainers were covered in bling.» What does bling mean here? | Wet from the rain | *Shiny, sparkly decoration | Dirty and muddy | A type of shoe
exercise: Ali says, «Her phone case is pure bling.» What does he mean? | It is very old and faded | *It is shiny and sparkly | It is broken and cracked | It is made for sleeping in
exercise: «He can't stop talking about his car, all bling and chains.» What does bling suggest about him? | Being cold in the winter | Feeling tired | *Showing off his wealth | Being very quiet
test: «The party was full of bling.» Which word could replace bling without changing the meaning much? | Mud | Silence | *Glitter | Puddle
test: Mia says, «My guy, that bling is wild!» What does my guy mean? | A famous singer | A stranger | *Mate | A jeweller
exam: Which sentence about bling is true? | It means very old and worn out | It means quiet and gloomy | *It is slang for shiny jewellery or a flashy show of wealth | It means a grey, wet day
